title: "thread under a Herdr parent: where its new session runs (S2)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Herdr
    lg1: None
    lg2: Path to the FirstInputSettles bug
    lg3: Repeats forever, so FirstInputSettles breaks
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 bugPath
  class lg3 repeats
  s0: No session row
  s1: Herdr row Pending, no pane yet
  s2: Herdr pane made, location not recorded
  s3: Herdr pane placed, not bound yet
  s4: Herdr execution retired
  s5: Herdr pane running
  s6: Herdr pane idle
  s7: Row deleted by thread_gc
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: a queued input starts the thread's session (turn host judges the host)
  s1 --> s2: Herdr creates the pane (answer may be lost)
  s1 --> s3: Herdr creates the pane (answer may be lost)
  s1 --> s4: unplaced row resolved: the pane adopted (not bound), or the row retired
  s2 --> s3: unplaced row resolved: the pane adopted (not bound), or the row retired
  s3 --> s3: the output reservation is made durable before the first key or the first input is submitted to the Herdr pane or AgentDesk restarts
  s4 --> s1: a queued input starts the thread's session (turn host judges the host)
  s3 --> s5: own SessionStart and source checked: the row binds
  s5 --> s6: the turn ends and the thread stays idle past an hour
  s6 --> s4: idle cleanup ends the session
  s4 --> s7: thread_gc deletes the row
  s7 --> s7: auto-queue resets the slot thread
